  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (ja): ダイジョ",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%80%E3%82%A4%E3%82%B8%E3%83%A7",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 106366634,
      "text": "ダイジョ（大薯、ダイショ）は、ヤムイモ（ヤマノイモ目ヤマノイモ科ヤマノイモ属の食用種）の1種の芋類。学名 Dioscorea alata。タメイモ（為芋）、シンショ（参薯）、デンショ（田薯）、コウシャイモ（拳薯）、オキナワヤマイモ（沖縄山芋）、タイワンヤマイモ（台湾山芋）、ウベ (フィリピン語：ube)、パープルヤム 、ウォーターヤム とも。奄美方言ではこうしゃまんという。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Dioscorea alata",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dioscorea_alata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1377984196,
      "text": "Dioscorea alata – also called ube, ubi, uwhi, purple yam, winged yam, or greater yam, among many other names – is a species of yam. The tubers are usually a vivid violet-purple to bright lavender, but some range from creamy-white to plain white. Although it is sometimes confused with taro and the Okinawa sweet potato beniimo , D. alata is also grown in Okinawa. Its origins are in the Asian and Oceanian tropics. Some varieties attain great size. A mambatap greater yam grown in Maprik, East Sepik Province, Papua New Guinea, around 1939 was 3.5 m (11 ft) in length."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Dioscorea alata",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dioscorea_alata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 171582010,
      "text": "El ñame de agua, ñame alado, tabena o en Filipinas ube o ubi es una especie de ñame que contiene pigmentos que dan color púrpura o violáceo."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Dioscorea alata",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dioscorea_alata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 240189674,
      "text": "Le Ube, igname ailée, grande igname ou cambarre est une espèce de plantes du genre Dioscorea et de la famille des Dioscoreaceae."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Dioscorea alata",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dioscorea_alata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 71404827,
      "text": "Dioscorea alata – também chamado de ube ou inhame-roxo, entre muitos outros nomes – é uma espécie de inhame da família Dioscoreaceae, originário do sudeste asiático e cultivado pelos seus tubérculos."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Ubi kelapa",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ubi_kelapa",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 29929952,
      "text": "Ubi kelapa atau ubi kenduduk adalah tanaman umbi-umbian yang bisa dimakan dan paling digemari daripada spesies lainnya dari genus Dioscorea. Ubi kelapa, ubi pasir, dan gembili lebih aman dimakan daripada gembolo dan gadung."
    }
  },
